<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see rain in the northwest.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see rain in the northwest.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Friday were forecast to see rain in the northwest, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see rain in the north, cloudiness in the central region and sun in the south with highs of 16 to 27 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see scattered showers in the west and sun in the east with highs of 21 to 26 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see a mix of sun and cloud with highs of 18 to 26 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
